            <p>1. <b>Sensor data</b> (Phase 6 simulation) and <b>historical readings</b> feed the overflow predictor when enough exist.<br>
            2. Where IoT history is thin, the <b>deterministic assumption model</b> (Phase 5/7) provides a fallback fill-rate signal — always labelled as such.<br>
            3. <b>Overflow prediction</b>: linear projection from recent fill-rate to 85%/95% thresholds.<br>
            4. <b>Priority scoring</b>: a transparent weighted sum of fill (30%), overflow risk (25%), weight (15%), time since collection (15%), and active-alert severity (15%) — shown factor-by-factor in the WHY panel.<br>
